 "youtube": {
  "title": "Duff Children: How Did 3 Kids Survive 9 Days Lost?",
  "description": "The Duff children were lost in the Australian bush for nine days in 1864. How did three kids survive, and who finally found them?\n\nIsaac (9), Jane (7) and little Frank (nearly 4) went to gather broom near their home in the Wimmera, Victoria, and wandered into the mallee scrub. More than 30 people searched until a thunderstorm washed away their tracks. On cold nights, Jane covered her little brother with her own dress. Then three Wotjobaluk trackers, Dick-a-Dick, Jerry and Fred, picked up the lost trail within hours, and all three children came home alive.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for one true survival story every day. Could you read a trail that thirty searchers missed? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #duffchildren #stickstory",
